# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-verification-runtime.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/546-sdlc-execute-stop-losing-time-to-idle-workers-restarts-and-truncated-gate-evidence/requirements.md
Feature: Execute keeps idle workers, prompts, restarts and gate evidence productive

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Idle worker without a handoff is resumed before any stage report
    Given a stage worker ends its turn without a fresh valid handoff and without a waiting marker
    When the controller observes the settled worker
    Then it delivers the handoff reminder to the same worker and issues no stage report before the resumed turn settles
    And the stage completes with the handoff from the resumed turn and no redispatch

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Stage report reflects the worker's last commit
    Given a worker's commit becomes visible after the worker first settles
    When the controller builds the stage report
    Then headAfter and commits include that commit

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Prompt reaches an idle worker or is refused with a reason code
    Given a stage report for an idle worker offers prompt
    When the supervisor answers prompt with guidance
    Then the worker's fresh handoff is used when it resumes
    And an undelivered prompt reports promptRefusal stage_prompt_undelivered
    And a prompt not started within 60 seconds reports promptRefusal stage_prompt_not_resumed without offering prompt

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Restart during a verify rerun at an unchanged head resumes verify
    Given a gate-intent record for head H and an earlier failed gate result at H
    And the controller was killed before verify completed
    When supervise resumes with HEAD at H
    Then it dispatches verify, not implement

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Accepted failed gate routes to implement
    Given the supervisor accepted a failed verify stage report at head H
    When routing runs at head H
    Then no gate-intent record exists and implement is dispatched

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Large gate output keeps failing test names and links the full log
    Given a command validation emits about 5 MB of output with pytest FAILED lines in its first 10%
    When the gate runner records the result
    Then the evidence entry lists the failing lines in failures and the summary
    And its artifact points to a log with the full output and its headSha matches HEAD

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Check-in during a running background command
    Given a stage worker's backgrounded Bash command is still running
    When the check-in interval elapses with no other activity
    Then the check-in names the command and its elapsed seconds in activity.background
    And its reason is not activity_unchanged
